WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.630
Why?

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:15.100
Why did it turn out like this?

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.120
We'll be starting soon too.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.710
I'm so excited.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:27.220
Our goal is just to complete the course.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.630
Let's have fun.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:29.510
Yeah!

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:32.630
Our goal is...

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:35.640
to have fun...

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.950
and to complete the course...

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.300
all together!

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:46.520
Okay, stop.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.470
We're putting a gap here.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:50.020
Huh?

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.900
Please wait for a bit.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.950
Huh?!

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.950
Oh my...

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:56.020
Well, it can't be helped.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:59.660
We'll go slowly.
So don't panic, just catch up to us.

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:03.660
See you up ahead.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.570
Don't worry, you'll catch up soon.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:09.340
Everyone!

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:16.970
I have to catch up to everyone quickly!

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:54.540
I can't see the cyclists I started out with.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.530
I-It's okay.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:01.530
They said they'll go slowly. It's okay.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:06.800
It's a long ride. I have to go at my own pace.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.340
So fast!

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.850
They're the pack from the back?

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:23.890
Huh? Hinako-san said the
time limit had a lenient buffer, but...

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.970
Don't tell me...

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:31.220
I won't make it unless I go that fast?!

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:37.730
Maybe going “slowly” doesn't mean this slowly.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:39.920
What do I do?

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:45.490
If I go at this pace,
I won't even catch up, let alone finish!

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:50.370
I have to go faster too!

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.630
They're going pretty fast!

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:08.080
Saki-chan, speed isn't our goal today.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.970
I know.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.770
I've been looking forward to today too.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.270
I wonder if Ami is all right.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:22.490
It's her first long ride and getting left behind alone like that...

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:24.050
I'm a little worried.

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:27.490
Maybe we should slow down just a tad more.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.620
Everyone!

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:38.710
Ami!

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:42.090
I caught up at last.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:46.340
Hey, why'd you pedal so hard?!

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:58.040
Ami, you okay?

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:02.160
Your legs cramped up.
You really overdid it.

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:07.770
Maybe we should take a longer break.

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:10.520
I think so. Ami, sit down.

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:13.520
Huh? No, I'm okay, so...

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.790
You're not okay at all.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:20.510
But, if we linger too long,
we won't be able to finish!

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:21.800
Listen...

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:26.300
If you ride in your condition,
you definitely won't finish.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:30.230
If you understand, rest.

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:31.190
Okay.

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:37.060
Here, hydrate.

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:40.060
Thank you.

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:43.940
Are we okay for time?

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:47.480
I told you there was a lenient buffer.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.860
What are you panicking about?

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:53.730
But the other cyclists are going so fast…

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:55.710
and we're getting left behind.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.630
Is that it?

00:05:57.630 --> 00:06:01.710
We can still easily make it
even if we go even slower.

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.960
Huh? Really?

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:08.350
We're pacing ourselves wisely so that we can finish.

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:09.720
Don't worry.

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:12.970
Oh, thank goodness.

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:15.500
It's your very first event.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:18.780
Don't worry about speed.
Let's take the time to enjoy this.

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:20.210
You're right.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:22.160
Sorry for the wait!

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:24.720
I got some...

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:26.990
for all of you!

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.500
We've been waiting!

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:31.740
Here.

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.140
What is it?

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:35.370
It's the replenishment from this aid station.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:36.520
Replenishment?

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:38.110
Just try it.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:45.880
Whoa! It's delicious! So sweet!

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:50.890
The stops where you can replenish energy and water are called aid stations.

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:55.390
There are several aid stations at long ride events.

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:58.110
The best part of the Azumino Autumn Ride...

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:02.300
are the delicious, nourishing treats at the aid stations.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:05.460
It's all free and all you can eat!

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:07.650
All you can eat?!

00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:11.530
Was Saki-san's true intent going after the food at the aid stations?

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.960
She's such a big eater.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.410
But I guess that's fine.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:18.510
Thanks to her, Ami's filled with energy again.

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:19.910
Seems like it.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.330
Are your legs feeling better?

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:25.560
Yes!

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:30.410
There's great food ahead too.
They're all fun spots.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.930
Look forward to it.

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:33.430
I will!

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:44.900
Oh, it's the second aid station already?

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.050
Yeah.

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:48.020
We're turning!

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:55.620
Umm...

00:07:57.750 --> 00:07:58.990
What's the matter?

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:02.750
I can keep going without resting.

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:05.720
Don't you want to eat?

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:10.630
I do, but we just stopped at the first station.

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:15.100
If we're going to finish the course,
maybe we should keep going.

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:16.830
Are you content with just finishing?

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:17.640
Huh?

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:20.310
The replenishment at Station Two...

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:22.770
is nothing to scoff at!

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:25.270
The rising steam...

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:27.520
That nostalgic aroma...

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:30.690
That soft, filling sensation in your mouth...

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:34.400
One bite and the flavor spreads in your mouth...

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:37.030
and seeps into your sweaty body.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:38.030
And then, you think...

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:42.780
Thank goodness I'm cycling!

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:46.790
It's the ultimate replenishment!

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:51.120
It's not an exaggeration to say it's
the most popular part of this Autumn Ride .

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.720
Any cyclist who finishes,

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:56.310
but neglects to eat this should be told...

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:00.680
Why the heck did you sign up for this ride anyway?!

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:06.190
So we'll stop at Aid Station Two, right?

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.560
Yes!

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:19.260
Wh-What's with this aid station?!

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:23.660
It's so far from the sign!

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:27.720
Well, it would be quite a shortcut
if we didn't take this detour.

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:30.280
But it's definitely worth it.

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:33.550
The replenishment at this second aid station...

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:35.620
is miso topped onigiri.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:43.920
What is this?! It's so good!

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:48.270
How can rice topped with only miso taste so amazing?!

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:51.630
See? Wasn't the detour worth it?

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:54.780
Yes! This is fantastic!

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:57.940
And there's much, much more to come.

00:09:57.940 --> 00:10:01.940
There's a lot more delicious food
waiting for us in the upcoming aid stations.

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:06.720
If there's so much delicious food...

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:10.750
I'll get fat from eating too much!

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:15.300
We're cycling a lot today.
So what if we overeat a little?

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:18.610
Yeah, I guess so.

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:20.680
We're just preventing hunger knocks, right?

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:26.010
Yes, exactly. We need to diligently
replenish our energy to avoid hitting the wall.

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:27.940
Saki, you just eat too much.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:35.460
I wonder what kind of food is next?

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:36.830
I can't wait.

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:41.570
Pickled food!

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:44.400
Delicious!

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:47.180
Ami, you took so much.

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:49.720
There's a huge pile over here too.

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:50.580
Is it?

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:55.590
They're all delicious, but the pickled turnips and carrots in particular stand out.

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:58.040
Hinako-chan, open wide.

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:01.220
Hey!

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:04.220
Stop it! It's embarrassing.

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:10.340
This! This is what I was waiting for!

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:11.660
It's so good.

00:11:11.660 --> 00:11:12.810
What's this?!

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:16.810
Paris-Brest! They only sell a limited quantity at the Autumn Ride.

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:22.540
Oh, this is too wonderful.

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:26.330
We're not done yet.
There are more gourmet spots coming up.

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:31.200
But I'm really starting to get full.

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:33.100
It's okay.

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:36.590
We're coming up to a lengthy high metabolism area soon.

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:40.590
High... metabolism... area?

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:53.230
H-How long does this up and down ride go on?

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:58.480
I told you it's a high metabolism area, didn't I?
Luckily, this is the only tough section.

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:03.490
Even if it's the only one... my legs are already

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:06.620
You'll be amazed at the next aid station.

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:10.340
They use only the freshest, local ingredients.

00:12:10.340 --> 00:12:14.120
Those elements mix together
to create a deep harmony of flavors

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:18.880
The exquisite taste is simply out of this world.

00:12:21.190 --> 00:12:23.440
But this ultimate dish is only granted

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:27.350
to those who climb this hill.

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:30.640
If you don't keep up, I'll eat it all!

00:12:34.510 --> 00:12:38.500
No! I'm going to eat too!

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:41.490
Once you get over this, it'll be downhill.

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:44.240
I'll do my best.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:46.500
Yeah, that's the spirit.

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:50.900
But this is really tough.

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:52.250
At times like this...

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:54.370
When going uphill...

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:57.580
Stand on your bike and look straight ahead.

00:12:58.140 --> 00:13:00.620
Shift into the lowest gear and slowly...

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:03.630
Wait! It's already on the lowest one?!

00:13:04.270 --> 00:13:07.390
But it's so hard to pedal..

00:13:09.170 --> 00:13:10.850
My legs...

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:11.640
Ami...

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:15.360
If it's too hard, it's okay to get off and push your bike.

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:18.720
If you overdo it here,
you won't be able to finish.

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:19.650
Okay.

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:21.650
But...

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:29.660
Everyone's having such an easy time.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:35.120
My goal is to participate in a flèche too!

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:37.650
It's just a little further!

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:46.840
I made it!

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:02.580
Aoi-chan said it's okay to push my bike.

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:05.990
I didn't lose...
Anyway, the goal is to finish...

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:12.740
Fortuna!

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:16.620
"Na"... A big serving of stir fried eggplant with meat-miso paste!

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:17.250
"Ri"...

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:21.250
Rear derailleur guide pulley.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.260
Ami!

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:31.100
Here she comes.

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:32.510
Hang in there!

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:38.540
E-Even pushing my bike was tough.

00:14:39.970 --> 00:14:41.360
Good job!

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:44.400
You did it. Make sure you hydrate.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:46.900
Yeah, thanks...

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:50.090
Okay, we'll go when Ami catches her breath.

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:51.180
Yes.

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:53.660
Okay, let's continue with our game of shiritori.

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:58.120
"Ri"... A big serving of beef curry with lots of apples!

00:14:58.120 --> 00:15:01.540
"Ri"... Rearside shifting lever.

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.840
Your turn, Aoi.  The sound is "A"...

00:15:05.270 --> 00:15:06.550
Huh? "A"...

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:07.800
Ami, right?

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:09.600
Ami!

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:12.800
Don't answer for me!

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:16.060
Everyone has so much energy left.

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:19.710
72 kilometers...

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:22.770
88 more to go.

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:25.190
That's not even halfway.

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:29.190
Will I be able to finish?

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:34.790
Good work, everyone.

00:15:45.140 --> 00:15:46.210
Wow!

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:50.170
This place gives me a sense of accomplishment, it feels like I've made it!

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:55.220
Right? We're at the turning point.
The Hakuba Jump Arena.

00:16:03.220 --> 00:16:04.610
Here, Ami.

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:06.610
Replenishment for this stop.

00:16:07.350 --> 00:16:09.860
Tonjiru pork soup!

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:16.740
I feel revived!

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:29.200
Miso topped onigiri on the way back?

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:32.380
Ami, what's wrong?

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:36.760
This is the turning point...
but we're only half way done.

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:39.860
I wonder if I can finish?

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:43.100
Don't worry! The return trip is mostly downhill

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:45.150
It won't be as tough.

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:48.660
Downhill... Then maybe I can...

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:51.840
Is it really?

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:53.400
It really is.

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:57.670
Hinako-san, you keep saying
not to worry or that it's easy...

00:16:57.670 --> 00:17:00.410
I've lost track of how many times
you've tricked me.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:03.410
But you want to ride it, right?

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:04.530
The flèche.

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:08.750
Then you can't lose spirit over something like this.

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:15.180
It's tough, but if you finish this,
you might see a whole new world.

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:17.930
A whole new world...

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:20.310
And delicious replenishment!

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:22.680
Delicious replenishment...

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:26.940
It's okay, Ami. We're all together with you.

00:17:27.530 --> 00:17:28.790
All together...

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:42.410
Yeah.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:52.880
Oh, it's so cool!

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:55.130
All right, let's speed it up!

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:58.330
It feels wonderful!

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:21.640
These jomon oyaki dumplings are amazing.

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:26.210
Nozawana greens are a staple,
but the hijiki seaweed and azuki beans are great too!

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:28.210
Try the pumpkin filling too.

00:19:28.210 --> 00:19:30.890
Just what I'd expect from you,
Saki-san, you know so much!

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:33.640
I've come here several times, that's why.

00:19:33.640 --> 00:19:37.150
I've tried them all, but today's taste the best.

00:19:38.510 --> 00:19:40.400
I'm always alone...

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:42.180
Eating with everyone...

00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:45.410
makes food taste even better.

00:19:46.230 --> 00:19:47.530
I agree!

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:50.970
When I'm together with everyone, the food, the fun,

00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:54.040
just about everything is way, way better!

00:19:55.620 --> 00:19:59.800
I'm amazed you all can say something that sappy without a hint of embarassment.

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:04.300
You say that, but, Hinako,
you're actually enjoying this the most, right?

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:06.060
That's right, isn't it?

00:20:06.060 --> 00:20:09.850
You've always wanted cycling friends.

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:12.100
What? It's not like that!

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:14.750
Hinako-san, you're blushing.

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:16.900
Want to share a dumpling?

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:18.110
No thanks!

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:24.990
But anyway, this Autumn Ride has been the best.

00:20:25.420 --> 00:20:27.450
I agree.

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:29.370
Oh, why?

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:31.550
I'm saying...

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:35.320
it's so much fun right now!

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:41.030
It's all because you formed Team Fortuna, Ami-chan.

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:43.380
Everyone...

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:45.660
Want to go for another round of dumplings?

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:46.880
Yes!

00:20:46.880 --> 00:20:50.890
But I'll definitely gain weight if I eat so much.

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:54.500
But it's so good, I can't stop!

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:58.080
Um...

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:03.150
Huh? Yes?

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:05.090
I'm event staff.

00:21:05.090 --> 00:21:09.160
You're really cutting it close on time. What'll you do?

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:12.580
Eh... what do you mean?

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:17.090
Oh, no... we got a little carried away.

00:21:17.090 --> 00:21:18.420
Looks like it.

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:21.580
We shouldn't have spent so much time eating.

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:25.050
No, this dumpling is a must-eat!

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:28.700
He's the event staff who rides behind the participants.

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:33.810
The fact that he's here means we're the last ones.

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:39.240
If we go over the time limit,
they'll close the finish line.

00:21:41.890 --> 00:21:43.190
D-Does that mean...

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:46.920
we won't be able to finish?!

00:23:30.570 --> 00:23:35.220
I nearly gave up a bunch of times,
but I'll do my best thanks to everyone's support!

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:40.020
But apparently we're the last ones! We have to hurry or we won't finish!

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:44.410
Next time on Long Riders: "The Azumino Autumn Ride! Part 2."
